<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-One tender of A$20.0 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES-One tender of A$20.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>One Australian commercial paper issuer held a tender on Thursday, selling A$20 million worth of promissory-notes.</p>
<p>General Property Trust made the three-month issue at roughly four basis points over BBSW.</p>
<p>Dealers said the bill curve had weakened over the morning on the back of lower U.S. Treasuries and continued speculation of an easing in monetary policy by the Reserve Bank of Australia.</p>
<p>&quot;Easings, no easings, (the market) just fluctuates with the mood,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Another said trade across the curve had been light, except for some fund interest in 90-day maturities.</p>
<p>At 11.25 a.m. (0025 GMT), March 90-day bank bill futures were trading at 94.40, down four points.</p>
